From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marcin Niestroj <m.niestroj@grinn-global.com>
Date: Fri, 26 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "ipc: set timeout value to 1"

This reverts an ATF change shipped in meta-synaptics v2.4.0
(synaptics commit 144d43e48fb1 squashed into astra-atf.patch by
8116214c "atf: ipc: set timeout value to 1") that reduced
IPC_MB_TIMEOUT in the Berlin secure-monitor mailbox driver from
10 ms to 1 us.

That timeout sits on the OPTEE -> ATF -> SCP path used for GPU
power-domain / clock changes on Astra (Dolphin / SL1680). 1 us is
far too short for the SCP to acknowledge a mailbox request: the
wait silently expires, ATF returns success anyway, and the Linux
side concludes the power transition completed when in reality the
GPU is still off.

Symptom on grinn-astra-1680-sbc: weston's first drm_pvr_srvkm_init
ioctl reaches RGXPostPowerState, the FW never sets bFirmwareStarted
within MAX_HW_TIME_US, the timeout path reads GPU status registers
on a dead GPU, the SoC/GPU AXI bridge raises an asynchronous SError
(impdef code 0xbf000002) and arm64 turns it into a panic.

Restore the original 10 ms timeout (1000*10) until Synaptics
provides a rationale or replacement for the v2.4.0 change.

Signed-off-by: Marcin Niestroj <m.niestroj@grinn-global.com>
---
 plat/syna/berlin/common/drivers/mailbox/sm_ipc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/plat/syna/berlin/common/drivers/mailbox/sm_ipc.c b/plat/syna/berlin/common/drivers/mailbox/sm_ipc.c
--- a/plat/syna/berlin/common/drivers/mailbox/sm_ipc.c
+++ b/plat/syna/berlin/common/drivers/mailbox/sm_ipc.c
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@
 #include "syna_ipc.h"
 #include "sm_ipc.h"
 
-#define IPC_MB_TIMEOUT (1)
+#define IPC_MB_TIMEOUT (1000*10)
 
 void sm_system_off(void)
 {
-- 
2.43.0

